<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>M1 Media Programming on Prof. Dr. Barne Kleinen</title><link>https://bkleinen.github.io/classes/ss2018/media-programming-rails/</link><description>Recent content in M1 Media Programming on Prof. Dr. Barne Kleinen</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://bkleinen.github.io/classes/ss2018/media-programming-rails/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>M1 Assignments</title><link>https://bkleinen.github.io/classes/ss2018/media-programming-rails/assignments/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bkleinen.github.io/classes/ss2018/media-programming-rails/assignments/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="web-frameworks"&gt;Web frameworks&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While developing the test application with your chosen framework, consider the following aspects of your chosen framework:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Routing and Architectural Patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How is HTML generated&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Authentication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Persistency and Connectivity to Databases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h1 id="github-repository"&gt;Github repository&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/htw-imi-m1/rails-todo-list-ss2018"&gt;https://github.com/htw-imi-m1/rails-todo-list-ss2018&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id="thema-todo-liste"&gt;Thema: Todo-Liste&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2 id="backlog"&gt;Backlog&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As a user, I can create an Entry in the Todo List&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As a user, I can delete an Entry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As a user, I can edit an Entry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As a user, I can mark an Entry as done&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As a user, I can see a list of all Todo Entries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As a user, I can filter all todo entries by 1. Category/Topic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As a user, I can mark an entry as important.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As a user, I can add a Category/Topic to an Todo 1. Entry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As a user, I can create a Category/Topic for Todo 1. Entries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As a user, I can see Todos sorted by due date.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As a user, I can add a due date to a todo entry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;</description></item><item><title>M1 Media Programming: Web Technology</title><link>https://bkleinen.github.io/classes/ss2018/media-programming-rails/web/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bkleinen.github.io/classes/ss2018/media-programming-rails/web/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="welcome"&gt;Welcome!&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This pages introduce you to the web application part of the &amp;ldquo;Epochenunterricht&amp;rdquo; in M1 Mediaprogramming.
The Epochenunterricht consists of 3 x 5 laboratory sessions for the three study focuses Web Technology,
Visual Computing and Game Technology respectively. Have a look at the &lt;a href="../overall-schedule"&gt;tentative overall schedule&lt;/a&gt; to
see how this breaks down.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="what-we-will-do"&gt;What we will do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within the five weeks of Web Technology, you will work on your own Web Application Project in a more or less
agile manner. Less agile, because you will work on the user stories not in the order of business value, but
in a technology driven order.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>M1 Overall Schedule</title><link>https://bkleinen.github.io/classes/ss2018/media-programming-rails/overall-schedule/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bkleinen.github.io/classes/ss2018/media-programming-rails/overall-schedule/</guid><description>&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;
